```
ROLE: theory_skeptic  VOTE: yellow
MUNDANE_EXPLANATIONS: [The 100pp gap is the textbook, pre-2020 result of "cache key over-specifies the equivalence class" — hashing transport bytes vs. post-canonicalization tensor is the same phenomenon as URL-vs-normalized-URL HTTP cache keys (RFC 7234 §2.2), content-hash vs. perceptual-hash in CDN dedup, and Merkle-keying raw vs. canonical IR in build systems (Bazel). The effect size (100pp on genuine lossless re-encodes) is not surprising — it is the DEFINITIONAL consequence of choosing the upstream domain as the key; any pre-key canonicalization step would close it. SGLang's 100% is therefore not evidence of a clever algorithm, only of keying one step later in the pipeline.]
CONFOUNDS: [(1) The 16.7% all-lossless number conflates a CORRECT hit (L4_base64_rewrap, byte-identical → SHOULD hit) with the false-miss class — the denominator mixes "no re-encode at all" with "genuine re-encode," inflating the apparent vLLM rate and making the strict-gate miss artifactual rather than mechanistic. (2) mm_processor_cache=ON 4GB default means measured "misses" are reproduction misses, not capacity misses — under realistic working-set pressure, processed-tensor caches (larger per entry — decoded float tensors vs. compressed bytes) may evict FASTER, partially erasing SGLang's advantage; this isn't measured. (3) "5 genuine re-encodes" is a hand-curated transform list, not a sample from a traffic distribution — selection bias toward transforms known to preserve pixels.]
ASSUMPTIONS_UNTESTED: [(a) That lossless pixel-preserving re-encoding has nonzero prevalence in real VLM traffic — entire headline rests on this, zero production telemetry cited. (b) That recovered hits translate to FLOPs/TTFT savings proportional to vision-encoder cost — L0 measures hit-rate only; the orchestrator note concedes this. (c) That processed-tensor hashing has equivalent collision/security properties to byte hashing (blake3 over bytes vs. hash over float tensors with potential nondeterminism from processor library/version drift — Qwen2VLImageProcessor upgrades could silently invalidate SGLang's cache while vLLM's would survive; this is a REVERSE confound not examined). (d) That the org-seam (source team injecting stable mm_uuid that survives re-encode) is actually harder than the SGLang-style fix — not benchmarked.]
STATISTICAL_GAPS: [N=320 images x 9 variants is adequate for a 0%-vs-100% effect (effect dwarfs any reasonable variance) so power is not the issue — but: no CI reported on the 16.7%; no per-variant breakdown of variance across the 320 images (are all images behaving identically per variant, or is there a tail?); no cross-run reproducibility (single CPU run, no seed sweep, no processor-version sensitivity); the blake3-vs-sha256 "0 disagreements / 2880" is descriptive, not a collision-probability bound. None of this changes the qualitative finding, but the packet overstates rigor by reporting point estimates without intervals.]
RATIONALE: Mechanism is real and the L0 is internally clean — honest lossy boundary holds (jpeg/resize → 0pp gap, correctly), and the cross-framework divergence (vLLM hasher.py vs. SGLang mm_utils.py hash_feature) is a verifiable code-level fact, not an inferred effect. The 100pp on genuine re-encodes is what basic cache-key theory predicts the moment you key one canonicalization step too early; that is the *strength* of the finding (clean mechanism) and simultaneously its *weakness* as a "discovery" (it's the expected consequence of a known anti-pattern, cf. cache-key over-specification in HTTP/CDN literature pre-2020). VOTE yellow, not red, because: the seam is empirically demonstrated, the null-exit was pre-registered and held, and the strict-gate miss is transparently disclosed with both denominators reported. VOTE yellow, not green, because the headline magnitude is entirely contingent on the UNMEASURED lossless-re-encode prevalence (the #1 stress-test), and the L0 cannot adjudicate that — it measures the gap conditional on the re-encode happening, not the marginal rate. Advance to L1 ONLY if L1 is scoped to (i) measure lossless-re-encode prevalence in a real VLM-serving trace (named source, not a synthetic transform list), (ii) convert recovered hits to FLOPs/TTFT under realistic working-set pressure with processed-tensor cache-size accounting, and (iii) test the reverse confound (processor-version drift invalidating processed-tensor hashes). Without (i)–(iii), advancing risks confirming a predicted-by-theory effect at unknown production magnitude.
```
